def dif_Square(n):
    """Write a python function to check whether the given number can be represented as difference of two squares or not.

    Since ``a**2 - b**2 == (a - b) * (a + b)`` and the two factors
    ``a - b`` and ``a + b`` always have the same parity, their product
    can never be congruent to 2 modulo 4. Conversely, every odd number
    ``n`` equals ``((n + 1) // 2)**2 - ((n - 1) // 2)**2`` and every
    multiple of four ``4k`` equals ``(k + 1)**2 - (k - 1)**2``. Taking
    the absolute value also covers negative numbers, whose representations
    are obtained by swapping the two squares.
    """
    return abs(n) % 4 != 2
